Adaptation is essential for addressing climate change challenges, minimizing vulnerabilities while mitigation reduces emissions. Both strategies are crucial, and adaptation investments are more effective when coupled with global mitigation efforts. Such investments protect health, infrastructure, and natural capital while requiring context-specific design and implementation to align with local needs. Not all adaptations necessitate significant financial outlays; integrating climate considerations into existing planning processes can enhance resilience cost-effectively. Immediate, low-regret options, such as disaster preparedness and urban greening, should be prioritized. Ultimately, proactive adaptation strategies will yield benefits that outweigh the costs of inaction, facilitating resilient economic growth and stability.
